# Modules as directories (claude/modules-style-pass.md): `A.Types` beside a top-level
# `Types`, each with a type `Amount`. A qualified name is a full path from the root, never
# relative, so inside `A` `Types.Amount` is the top-level one: the C++ target qualifies every
# reference from the global namespace (an inner `a::types` would hide `types`), and the
# Rust one by its path from the crate (`a/mod.rs` declares `pub mod types`).
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod A
mod Types
test mod Tests
use Ui

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{A.Describe 3}")
